{
    "background_story": "Brennan was a master bookbinder with a passion for preserving the written word. Growing up in a family of printers and publishers, he learned the art of bookbinding from his father. After completing his apprenticeship, Brennan set up his own workshop in a quaint town square, where he spent his days meticulously crafting leather-bound tomes and repairing rare volumes. His attention to detail and dedication to his craft earned him a reputation among book collectors and authors. Brennan's most prized project was a limited edition of a classic novel, which he bound in hand-tooled leather and adorned with intricate gold filigree. His work was not only functional but also beautiful, a testament to the enduring power of the written word. As a bookbinder, Brennan felt a deep connection to the stories and knowledge contained within the pages he so carefully preserved.",
